To use a custom domain with GitHub Pages (free hosting, ~$10-15/yr for the domain):

1. Buy a domain from any registrar (Cloudflare, Namecheap, etc.)
2. Rename this file to `CNAME` (no extension)
3. Replace this entire file content with just your domain name:
     kishoresudhamalla.design
4. At your registrar, add DNS records pointing to GitHub Pages:
   - Apex domain → 4 A records: 185.199.108.153 / .109.153 / .110.153 / .111.153
   - Subdomain (e.g. portfolio.yourdomain.com) → CNAME to <username>.github.io
5. In GitHub repo: Settings → Pages → enter the domain, enable Enforce HTTPS
6. Leave ASTRO_SITE and ASTRO_BASE repo variables unset (root `/` is the correct base)
